          "question": "Brought up something that looked like old coffee grounds this morning after a night of retching.",
          "answer": "**Call emergency services now, or go to the nearest emergency department.** Vomit that looks like coffee grounds can be a sign of bleeding in the upper digestive tract. The Gastrointestinal bleeding guidance (red-flag-gastrointestinal-bleeding) lists it under \"Call emergency services immediately.\" Don't wait to see whether it happens again.\n\nThe automated risk check returned \"routine\" because this exact wording wasn't in its fixed list. That result is not reassurance, and the guidance above takes priority.\n\nWhile you wait for help:\n- Don't drive yourself. Ask someone to stay with you.\n- Sit or lie down. If you feel faint, lie down with your legs raised.\n- Don't eat or drink anything until a clinician has assessed you.\n- Tell the emergency staff what you saw, when it started, and about any medicines you take, especially blood thinners.\n\nThe guidance also says to call emergency services straight away if you have dizziness, faintness, collapse, a racing or pounding heartbeat, cold clammy skin, confusion, or shortness of breath. It also lists black, tarry stools as an emergency sign.\n\nThis is general information, not a diagnosis. Only a clinician who examines you can tell what is causing this.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
